# etude-5dr.3 plan — atomic caller runner capability and guard

## Goal and boundary

Ship issue #15 in one commit and one PR. A stage may explicitly run in the exact
directory from which the CLI was invoked, while omitted or `hermetic` workspace
retains the detached worktree. Gates remain unchanged in the original pinned
detached checkout. The executed workspace and post-run commit are recorded in
the stage manifest.

ANCESTOR: etude-5dr (P1) — another project is blocked on Etude producing work in
the caller's live tree, and the issue requires the capability and mutation guard
to ship together. The deciding measurement is that a runner leaving tracked,
staged, or non-ignored untracked residue must fail before output capture or gate
execution, while a clean runner-created commit succeeds and is recorded.

BLAST RADIUS: changes are limited to this Etude worktree, Etude run refs created
for review evidence, and disposable Git repositories used for verification. The
manual proof builds the repository CLI and invokes that local binary; it does not
install packages, alter shared services, or push to main. The final branch and
review refs are pushed only for the requested pull request.

TRUST BOUNDARY: workflow configuration, the resolved repository root, Git, and
the authorized runner are trusted. The runner is trusted not to deliberately
forge Git internals or replace Git/tooling solely to defeat inspection; this is a
state-ordering guard, not a sandbox for hostile code already holding the
operator's filesystem permissions. Runner output and ordinary working-tree
effects are untrusted until Git reports a stable committed HEAD and clean state.
Repositories with tracked submodules are rejected before the runner because a
top-level inspection cannot bind arbitrary nested Git controls and index state.

TOPOLOGY: one Etude engine invokes one producing runner synchronously at the
single stage-execution site. The runner may start child processes, but background
writers that outlive its successful return and unrelated concurrent repository
writers are outside the caller-runner contract; callers must provide exclusive
working-tree access. Repeated status/control checks bounded by stable HEAD reads
still fail closed on instability observed during provenance capture.

DURABILITY CLASS: caller runner effects are at-least-once across a crash before
stage capture; successful stage publication remains one append protected by the
existing compare-and-swap ref update. The authoritative generation identity is
the Git commit SHA resolved after the runner, not the invocation-time SHA or a
timestamp proxy.

IRREVERSIBLE SEQUENCE caller-runner: 1 steps
IRREVERSIBLE STEP caller-runner.1: invoke the authorized producing runner in the caller working tree

If the process stops during or after the runner, runner-side edits or a clean
commit may remain without a stage record. This existing at-least-once frontier
behavior is documented; the operator reconciles the live tree before resuming.

## Design

1. Add a validated runner `workspace` enum. Absent/`hermetic` remains the current
   behavior; `caller` is opt-in. Preserve default-runner inheritance,
   workspace-only overlays, and CLI `--runner` command overrides.
2. Capture the CLI's exact invocation directory and pass it only to producing
   caller runners. Keep provenance inspection anchored at the stable repository
   root even if the runner commits deletion or movement of the invocation path.
3. Before invoking a caller runner, reject tracked gitlinks and snapshot both
   repository-local control files and Git's effective local configuration with
   includes. After successful runner completion, repeatedly verify unchanged
   controls, reject assume-unchanged/skip-worktree paths, require repository-wide
   porcelain status to be empty with all untracked paths and submodule dirtiness
   visible, and require HEAD to remain identical across the inspection. Perform
   artifact storage, run-ref capture, and gate execution only after this passes.
4. Permit a runner-created clean commit and record its post-run SHA plus
   `runner_workspace: caller`. Emit manifest v4 only when the new field is used;
   preserve and validate legacy versions otherwise. Render the choice in
   human-readable `run show`.
5. Leave gate directory and pinned SHA wiring unchanged and test it explicitly.
   Document syntax, inheritance, post-run cleanliness, unsupported submodules,
   dirty/crash residue, manifest audit data, and gate isolation.

## Complete sites

COMPLETENESS ENUMERATION: all initial, resume, and gate-rerun stage executions converge on
`Engine.runAndCaptureStage`, so workspace selection and the guard live at that
single producing-runner site. Workflow parsing/validation, runner resolution,
CLI construction, manifest serialization/versioning, and run-show rendering are
the remaining configuration/audit sites. Replay, standalone gates, checks, and
model seats do not opt into caller workspace and remain hermetic.

## Planned regressions

Planned regression: caller workspace parsing, validation, default inheritance,
workspace-only overlay, explicit hermetic override, and round trip.

Planned regression: default runners still receive the detached worktree and
legacy manifests retain their prior versions and bytes.

Planned regression: CLI invocation from a repository subdirectory runs there,
and `--runner` preserves caller workspace.

Planned regression: a caller runner may make a clean commit, whose post-run SHA
and caller workspace appear in the v4 manifest and `run show`.

Planned regression: unstaged, staged, and non-ignored untracked residue each
fail the stage before artifact/ref capture; ignored files remain permitted.

Planned regression: index visibility flags, changes to raw or included local Git
controls, and a changing HEAD fail closed.

Planned regression: repositories containing tracked submodules fail before the
runner is invoked.

Planned regression: a runner that adds and commits a tracked submodule fails
after execution but before stage capture.

Planned regression: a caller runner can commit deletion of its invocation
directory because provenance checks remain anchored at the repository root.

Planned regression: a caller stage gate still executes in the original pinned
detached worktree rather than the caller tree or its new commit.

## Verification

Run focused package tests, `make test`, `make lint`, `make docs-check`, and
`make docs-reality`. Build the actual CLI and use disposable repositories to
prove default hermetic success, caller clean-commit success with manifest audit
data, and caller tracked-mutation failure without capture or gate execution.
